# XCU eval
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/eval.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.eval.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall construct a command string by concatenating
class      required
says       eval joins its operands with single spaces into one command
           string and executes it.
test       t/001-concatenate.sh

assertion  XCU.eval.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/in the current
class      required
says       The constructed command runs in the current shell environment:
           variables, functions and positional parameters it sets stay set.
test       t/002-current-env.sh

assertion  XCU.eval.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXAMPLES/foo=10 x=foo
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall construct a command string by concatenating
class      required
says       The operands are expanded once by the shell and the result is
           parsed again, so eval y='$'$x with x holding a variable name
           gives y that variable's value.
test       t/003-double-expansion.sh

assertion  XCU.eval.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/exit status of the command defined
class      required
says       The exit status of eval is that of the command it executes.
test       t/004-status.sh

assertion  XCU.eval.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/or only null <i>argument</i>s
class      required
says       eval with no operands, or only null operands, returns status zero
           even when the previous status was not zero.
test       t/005-no-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.eval.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/tokenized
class      required
says       The command string is tokenized and parsed as shell language:
           reserved words, lists and quoting in it work as in a script.
test       t/006-parsed-afresh.sh

assertion  XCU.eval.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/could not be parsed
class      required
says       A syntax error in the constructed command makes a non-interactive
           shell exit with a non-zero status without running later commands.
test       t/007-syntax-error.sh
